From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] core: a switch for importance-watch ports

Before it execs a job that has MachServices, launchd's forked child asks
PID 1 for send rights to them (get_listener_port_rights) and passes them to
posix_spawn(2) as importance-watch ports, so that a message to one boosts
the daemon. PID 1 answers with an out-of-line array of made send rights
(job.defs: mach_port_make_send_array_t). xnu-12377 refuses that from a
platform binary (IPC_POLICY_ENHANCED_V2: only COPY_SEND arrays, and only to
ports that accept arrays, which a MIG reply port never does) with a fatal
guard exception: starting com.apple.auditd, NeoDarwin's first on-demand
daemon, killed PID 1 (EXC_GUARD, kGUARD_EXC_DESCRIPTOR_VIOLATION) and the
kernel panicked (docs/base/session.md, "BSM audit"). Add
HAVE_IMPORTANCE_WATCH_PORTS (config.h; default 1, so 842's behaviour) around
the child's request, so the build can leave it out; the daemon then runs
unboosted, as a job without MachServices does.

Rebase-risk: low (one #if, kr declared ahead of it, and one config.h switch).
---
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -42,6 +42,14 @@
 #define HAVE_PER_USER_LAUNCHD !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
 #endif
 
+/* Importance-watch ports: a job's child asks launchd for send rights to the
+ * job's MachServices (get_listener_port_rights) and passes them to
+ * posix_spawn(2), so that messages to them boost the daemon.
+ */
+#ifndef HAVE_IMPORTANCE_WATCH_PORTS
+#define HAVE_IMPORTANCE_WATCH_PORTS 1
+#endif
+
 #ifndef HAVE_SYSTEMSTATS
 #if !TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED && __has_include(<systemstats/systemstats.h>)
 #define HAVE_SYSTEMSTATS 1
--- a/src/core.c
+++ b/src/core.c
@@ -4653,9 +4653,11 @@
 	        j->jetsam_priority, j->jetsam_memlimit));
 #endif
 
+	kern_return_t kr;
+#if HAVE_IMPORTANCE_WATCH_PORTS
 	mach_port_array_t sports = NULL;
 	mach_msg_type_number_t sports_cnt = 0;
-	kern_return_t kr = vproc_mig_get_listener_port_rights(bootstrap_port, &sports, &sports_cnt);
+	kr = vproc_mig_get_listener_port_rights(bootstrap_port, &sports, &sports_cnt);
 	if (kr == 0 && sports_cnt) {
 		/* For some reason, this SPI takes a count as a signed quantity. */
 		(void)posix_spawnattr_set_importancewatch_port_np(&spattr, (int)sports_cnt, sports);
@@ -4673,6 +4675,7 @@
 	} else if (kr != BOOTSTRAP_UNKNOWN_SERVICE) {
 		(void)job_assumes_zero(j, kr);
 	}
+#endif /* HAVE_IMPORTANCE_WATCH_PORTS */
 
 #if TARGET_OS_EMBEDDED
 	if (!j->app || j->system_app) {
